cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: "Certified spin, mass and horizons of the Bowen-York spinning puncture family"
authors:
  - name: "Moki & Julio"
version: "1.0"
license: CC-BY-4.0
keywords:
  - Bowen-York initial data
  - spinning black holes
  - numerical relativity
  - Lichnerowicz equation
  - Hamiltonian constraint
  - maximal spin
  - extreme initial data
  - computer-assisted proof
  - interval arithmetic
  - rigorous numerics
abstract: >-
  Conformally flat Bowen-York data for a single spinning puncture cannot describe a rapidly spinning black hole: the
  spin ratio J/M_ADM^2 stays below about 0.93. We certify this with interval arithmetic for every spin and every
  puncture mass mu > 0: a uniform ceiling J/M_ADM^2 <= 0.962234888831116 (P2c), then the supremum of the family in
  [0.9282004538, 0.9282004687], so it rounds to 0.928200 (P2e), and, directly on the throat of the extreme (mu = 0)
  data, chi(0) in [0.92820045875619, 0.92820045878266] (B3T). Every load-bearing certificate is blind-replicated by
  an independent formulation. Every sealed test is listed, including one FAILED blind replication and its re-test.
  Code, exact-rational results and reproduction scripts included.
